# Strings & constants

## UI strings
- Never hardcode user-facing strings in Kotlin (screens, VMs, snackbars, notifications, dialogs).
- Add every new string to `shared/src/commonMain/composeResources/values/strings.xml` (default **en**).
- Do **not** auto-translate other locales (`values-hi`, `values-bn`, etc.) unless the user asks — leave translations for manual follow-up.
- Reference strings via Compose Resources / `UiText` / existing i18n helpers, not raw `"..."`.

## Constants
- Never scatter magic strings/numbers for prefs keys, shop ids, language codes, notification channels, delays, etc.
- Put shared app-wide constants in `shared/.../util/AppConstants.kt` (`object AppConstants`).
- Create or extend `AppConstants` when a new shared constant is needed; prefer reusing existing entries over duplicating.
- Feature-private constants may stay as `private const` in that feature/file when they are not reused.
